{"id": "EUVD-2026-108681", "enisaUuid": "874aac1a-e46d-3f63-b24e-c64f67fcdeef", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: mac80211_hwsim: reject undersized HWSIM_ATTR_TX_INFO\n\nhwsim_tx_info_frame_received_nl() casts the HWSIM_ATTR_TX_INFO payload\nto a struct hwsim_tx_rate * and unconditionally reads\nIEEE80211_TX_MAX_RATES entries (8 bytes) from it. The policy only bounds\nthe attribute from above (NLA_BINARY .len is a maximum) and the op sets\nGENL_DONT_VALIDATE_STRICT, so a short or zero-length attribute is\naccepted and the loop reads past the payload.\n\nRequire the exact length in the policy, so a malformed attribute is\nrejected before the handler runs.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T11:37:44", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T11:37:44", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3a96bb65b4b820d8b41fa155781ec1c29e3479d4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/59e1f2a0242232b4a3af144ae317d3913fc09046", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ae85bb34fe3510659b86d6a5f8036dd498233f8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6f6368b20f8c9481fa7ba7b672dcb3c9f36b2695", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b5b1234bbfa25537fb9a5c0d62c328ed4547f721", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/13edd8ea7ff2ce6a964b290ef2034cd8cbed96c7", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3dc723ac78a6e4fa0fd49e27e487ed319da40a9f"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98887"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02168acf-e1d5-38d8-bf9c-923c2f8539fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <6f6368b20f8c9481fa7ba7b672dcb3c9f36b2695"}, {"id": "0add340f-5cd6-3da3-ae58-e47d136cbb91", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "0f44b85e-4ca4-3f56-971f-bbb6b26fed0b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "0 <5.15.222"}, {"id": "126e4298-338b-3410-9c48-e420347b91ef", "product